WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.735
-Earlier tonight,
I got to talk to my first guest

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:04.037
about today's events.

00:00:04.037 --> 00:00:05.971
He's a multiple Emmy and Peabody
Award-winning journalist

00:00:05.971 --> 00:00:07.540
and "The New York Times"
best-selling author

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.175
of "What Unites Us."

00:00:09.175 --> 00:00:13.612
Here is my conversation with
the one and only Dan Rather.

00:00:13.612 --> 00:00:17.416
Dan, thank you so much
for being here tonight.

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.018
-Jimmy, thank you
for having me on.

00:00:19.018 --> 00:00:21.954
It's a privilege and an honor
to be with you. Thank you.

00:00:21.954 --> 00:00:23.656
-We thought the big news
of the day

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:25.692
was going to be
how things went in Georgia

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:28.194
and with
the electoral-vote count,

00:00:28.194 --> 00:00:32.665
but then this afternoon, Trump
supporters stormed the Capitol.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:35.534
And we're talking a few hours
before this will air,

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.570
but could you give us
a breakdown

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:40.139
of what happened today
and where things stand now

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:43.776
as events continue to unfold?

00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:45.845
-Well, things are continuing
to unfold.

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:48.047
During the evening,
I expect they will continue

00:00:48.047 --> 00:00:50.750
even deep into
the early morning hours

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:53.719
because this has been
an absolutely --

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:57.289
and frequently overworked word
but an apt word in this case.

00:00:57.289 --> 00:00:59.859
This is an absolutely
unprecedented situation

00:00:59.859 --> 00:01:04.230
for our country and one --
and a very serious situation.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:08.701
Basically what happened was
that, increasingly, it appeared

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:12.238
that the two Democratic
candidates were winning

00:01:12.238 --> 00:01:16.108
and had won the Senate
runoff races in Georgia.

00:01:16.108 --> 00:01:18.111
This would, of course,
mean that the Democrats

00:01:18.111 --> 00:01:19.946
would have effective control
of the Senate

00:01:19.946 --> 00:01:22.015
in the new Biden administration.

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:25.318
So, that news didn't
really get solidified

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:28.220
until the wee hours
of early this morning.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.023
After that,
there was a rally planned

00:01:31.023 --> 00:01:34.727
in front of the White House,
a pro-Trump rally.

00:01:34.727 --> 00:01:37.530
The President --
I use the word "incited" it.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:39.365
You can't use any other word.

00:01:39.365 --> 00:01:42.001
Incited the crowd
to march down to the Capitol

00:01:42.001 --> 00:01:44.537
and to force a delay

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.139
in the certification
of Biden's victory.

00:01:47.139 --> 00:01:49.775
That was to be the other
big headline of the day.

00:01:49.775 --> 00:01:52.278
The big headline of the day
was expected to be Democrats

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.547
win two Senate races in Georgia

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:59.085
and the combined Congressional
power in the country

00:01:59.085 --> 00:02:03.489
certifying
the final electoral votes.

00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:08.294
Even as Vice President Pence
was presiding in the chamber

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.597
and the final certification
of the Biden victory

00:02:11.597 --> 00:02:13.566
was getting under way,

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:17.436
then this crowd
stormed the U.S. Capitol.

00:02:17.436 --> 00:02:20.472
You can describe it
as "protesters," if you like.

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:23.576
I, myself, think
they were certainly rioters.

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.611
They broke windows.
They were violent.

00:02:25.611 --> 00:02:27.179
They stormed the Capitol.

00:02:27.179 --> 00:02:30.916
They stormed actually
into the room where --

00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:33.418
the chamber, where
the deliberation was happening.

00:02:33.418 --> 00:02:35.955
All hell broke loose.

00:02:35.955 --> 00:02:38.858
There was no law and there
was no order for a while.

00:02:38.858 --> 00:02:40.726
You had mob violence

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:43.462
inside the Capitol
of the United States.

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:47.700
Now finally the law-enforcement
officers, first of all,

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.168
they got some reinforcements.

00:02:49.168 --> 00:02:52.337
Secondly, they sort of
solidified their own response.

00:02:52.337 --> 00:02:54.507
And most, if not all,

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:59.012
of what I call the rioters
were put outside the Capitol.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:01.915
It's a little hard to say what
the situation is at this moment,

00:03:01.915 --> 00:03:04.083
and I emphasize that it's fluid.

00:03:04.083 --> 00:03:05.518
But here's the thing, Jimmy.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:09.221
We have never seen this
in our country before --

00:03:09.221 --> 00:03:11.490
an effort to overthrow

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.294
the legitimate vote
of the people

00:03:14.294 --> 00:03:16.162
in a presidential election.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:19.065
This was by
any dictionary definition

00:03:19.065 --> 00:03:22.234
a coup attempt, which is to say,

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.138
"Okay, we've had an election.

00:03:25.138 --> 00:03:26.672
We, this mob, we don't agree

00:03:26.672 --> 00:03:28.474
with the outcome
of the election,

00:03:28.474 --> 00:03:31.177
which even the courts
have certified in their own way.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:33.045
And we're going to overturn it."

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:35.648
That's a definition of a coup,
and I do think

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:39.819
this could be described
as a case of domestic violence.

00:03:39.819 --> 00:03:42.521
Not everybody in this crowd
of people were violent today.

00:03:42.521 --> 00:03:44.157
Not nearly everybody.

00:03:44.157 --> 00:03:46.693
But there certainly
were outright rioters

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:49.395
who were taking part
in domestic violence,

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.398
and the overall scene
was one of a coup attempt.

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:56.035
It has failed.
That's pretty much where we are.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:04:00.005
-Do you think there will be
charges against these people?

00:04:00.005 --> 00:04:02.008
-Well, let's be very clear.
There should be

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:05.378
because if you break windows
in the U.S. Capitol

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:07.714
and go in and occupy the offices

00:04:07.714 --> 00:04:10.182
of elected representatives
of the country,

00:04:10.182 --> 00:04:12.218
those are crimes.

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:14.420
Whether they will be
prosecuted or not,

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.756
frankly, I have my doubts
as time goes along.

00:04:17.756 --> 00:04:21.327
But there is a movement
to try to identify those people

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:24.396
who were actually breaking
windows and occupying offices

00:04:24.396 --> 00:04:26.032
and bring charges against them.

00:04:26.032 --> 00:04:28.968
But the real important question
of the moment, Jimmy,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:32.004
and I think this will play out
over the next few days,

00:04:32.004 --> 00:04:36.976
is what is to be done about the
president of the United States?

00:04:36.976 --> 00:04:39.478
Make no mistake --
there are talks in the Capitol

00:04:39.478 --> 00:04:43.716
among some Republicans,
including some Democrats,

00:04:43.716 --> 00:04:47.286
of should some move be made
to remove President Trump

00:04:47.286 --> 00:04:50.255
from office
in just his last 13 days?

00:04:50.255 --> 00:04:53.892
He only has 13 more days
in office.

00:04:53.892 --> 00:04:56.128
That shows you how serious
the situation is.

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:58.631
I'm not saying that any
of that's going to happen.

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.633
You know, under the 25th
Amendment to the Constitution,

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:03.235
if the Vice President

00:05:03.235 --> 00:05:06.772
and a majority
of the cabinet secretaries

00:05:06.772 --> 00:05:09.542
agree that the President
is not capable

00:05:09.542 --> 00:05:13.679
or won't carry out his duties,
then they can ask the Congress

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.448
to have a vote in both houses
to remove the President.

00:05:16.448 --> 00:05:17.983
That's a major step.

00:05:17.983 --> 00:05:19.452
I wouldn't go so far as to say

00:05:19.452 --> 00:05:21.453
that we can expect
that step to happen,

00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:24.457
but it gives you an indication,
again, of how serious this is,

00:05:24.457 --> 00:05:26.893
when you have
that kind of serious talk

00:05:26.893 --> 00:05:29.829
in the Capitol
of the United States.

00:05:29.829 --> 00:05:33.232
It's the result
of this unprecedented day

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:35.767
in which as a country,
as a people,

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:38.203
we embarrassed ourselves.
-How --

00:05:38.203 --> 00:05:39.939
-In the eyes of the world,

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:42.875
we clearly embarrassed
ourselves.

00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:46.912
-How much is President Trump
to blame for what happened today

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:50.349
and who else is to blame?

00:05:50.349 --> 00:05:52.752
-Well, I'll give you
my opinion, Jimmy,

00:05:52.752 --> 00:05:54.887
but, you know, I always like
to be straight with you.

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:57.289
There are plenty of people
who have other opinions,

00:05:57.289 --> 00:05:59.992
but I think that history
is going to judge

00:05:59.992 --> 00:06:03.262
that President Trump
primarily is responsible

00:06:03.262 --> 00:06:05.031
for what happened today.

00:06:05.031 --> 00:06:07.366
The power of the presidency

00:06:07.366 --> 00:06:12.337
is a power
to inspire and/or to incite.

00:06:12.337 --> 00:06:15.507
And, clearly, President Trump
has been trying to incite

00:06:15.507 --> 00:06:17.176
just this kind of action.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.778
There's no -- You know,

00:06:18.778 --> 00:06:21.380
I don't see that there's
any real argument about it.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.749
The argument can be, "Well,
he was justified in doing it,"

00:06:23.749 --> 00:06:25.518
which is a false argument.

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:28.054
But the direct answer
to your question --

00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:31.057
that the buck starts
with President Trump,

00:06:31.057 --> 00:06:33.358
and it goes through
those members of his party,

00:06:33.358 --> 00:06:35.128
the Republican Party.

00:06:35.128 --> 00:06:36.962
Not all members
of the Republican Party,

00:06:36.962 --> 00:06:42.068
but, really, a large majority of
members of the Republican Party

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:45.137
have aided
and abetted the President

00:06:45.137 --> 00:06:50.042
in convincing a large section
of the American public

00:06:50.042 --> 00:06:53.512
that Joe Biden would be
an illegitimate president,

00:06:53.512 --> 00:06:55.581
that the election
was not legitimate

00:06:55.581 --> 00:06:57.750
and Biden wasn't
legitimately elected.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:06:59.151
It started with the President.

00:06:59.151 --> 00:07:03.556
It goes through
his enablers and allies

00:07:03.556 --> 00:07:06.191
and people within
the Republican Party.

00:07:06.191 --> 00:07:10.562
And then, again, frankly,
Jimmy, none of us can say

00:07:10.562 --> 00:07:13.099
that we don't share
at least some of the blame

00:07:13.099 --> 00:07:15.334
because we have let this happen.

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.170
We have reached
this point in our history

00:07:17.170 --> 00:07:20.539
where we have
an undisciplined mob,

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:23.408
including some rioters
and domestic terrorism,

00:07:23.408 --> 00:07:25.211
storming our own Capitol.

00:07:25.211 --> 00:07:26.878
Exclamation point.

00:07:26.878 --> 00:07:29.648
-Were you surprised to see
how easy it was for them

00:07:29.648 --> 00:07:31.817
to break into the Capitol?

00:07:31.817 --> 00:07:33.385
-I was surprised.

00:07:33.385 --> 00:07:36.655
Perhaps, I shouldn't have been,
but I thought, frankly,

00:07:36.655 --> 00:07:39.425
that a combination
of the Capitol police

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:42.795
and the Washington police
and federal forces,

00:07:42.795 --> 00:07:45.130
such as the FBI and others,

00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:49.334
would have a plan
for meeting this kind of effort

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:52.071
to a mob take over the Capitol,

00:07:52.071 --> 00:07:53.772
so I was surprised

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:56.709
that law enforcement
was not more effective.

00:07:56.709 --> 00:07:59.478
In the early going,
it was not effective at all.

00:07:59.478 --> 00:08:01.914
But before we criticize
the law-enforcement officers,

00:08:01.914 --> 00:08:04.150
I want to know
what instructions they had.

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:06.118
I don't know what instructions
they had.

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:08.821
In the early going, they just --
they fled the mob.

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:10.956
They just --
They absolutely fled.

00:08:10.956 --> 00:08:13.192
They just fled --
The law-enforcement officers,

00:08:13.192 --> 00:08:17.429
that Capitol police, and others
there just fled the scene.

00:08:17.429 --> 00:08:20.566
After a while, they began
to try to get control,

00:08:20.566 --> 00:08:23.668
but in the early going,
the performance was very poor.

00:08:23.668 --> 00:08:28.674
But, again, that may be
on orders from some other place,

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:31.744
including, you know,
somebody in the Capitol

00:08:31.744 --> 00:08:33.245
who's in charge of the force.

00:08:33.245 --> 00:08:35.247
We just have to see.

00:08:35.247 --> 00:08:37.850
But, you know,
as we speak now, Jimmy,

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:40.887
the National Guard
has been called in.

00:08:40.887 --> 00:08:42.988
I think a strong case
could be made

00:08:42.988 --> 00:08:45.958
given the consequences of today
that the National Guard

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:49.795
should have been standing by
as this day started

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:52.464
because President Trump had
already scheduled that rally.

00:08:52.464 --> 00:08:56.836
But nonetheless, order is
being restored in the Capitol.

00:08:56.836 --> 00:08:59.237
The National Guard is now there.

00:08:59.237 --> 00:09:01.640
Things will probably
simmer down somewhat

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.009
over the next 12 to 24 hours,

00:09:04.009 --> 00:09:06.945
but we as a country,
as a people,

00:09:06.945 --> 00:09:10.482
we're stuck with the question,
"What do we do now?"

00:09:10.482 --> 00:09:12.384
We know this is embarrassing.

00:09:12.384 --> 00:09:14.452
We know this is not
the American way.

00:09:14.452 --> 00:09:16.021
We know it's perilous.

00:09:16.021 --> 00:09:19.258
It's very dangerous
to have this situation prevail.

00:09:19.258 --> 00:09:20.959
So the question is,
what do we do now?

00:09:20.959 --> 00:09:23.028
-There's lots more
I want to talk to you about.

00:09:23.028 --> 00:09:24.730
More with Dan Rather
when we come back

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.265
to "The Tonight Show,"
everybody.

00:09:26.265 --> 00:09:27.533
-Thank you, Jimmy.

